<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phanariotes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Phanariots</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Phanariotes were members of wealthy Greek families of the Phanar, the Greek quarter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarchate</a>. From the late 17th century they served the Ottoman state as dragomans, and from the 1710s the sultans appointed them princes of Moldavia and Wallachia, until the Greek revolt of 1821. Phanariotes also governed the autonomous Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phanariotes.jpg" alt="Phanariotes" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fanarion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
